  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1237 PM CDT Wed Oct 21 2026\n\nThe upper low will become elongated and split beginning Friday. This \nwill somewhat inhibit moisture advection into our area and it now\nlooks as though conditions will remain completely dry everywhere \nthrough Friday evening. A full closed low will become completely \ncutoff over SoCal/southern AZ by Saturday. Models indicate it \ndipping a bit farther south from yesterday, thus the majority of \nshower and thunderstorm chances through Saturday evening would be \nconfined to the TX/NM border. As the low lifts north and eastward \nSaturday night into Sunday, the southerly moisture fetch out \nahead of it will shift concurrently eastward as well. The heavy \nrain threat will still primarily remain on the Caprock through \nmuch of Sunday. The low will stay cutoff as it turns more due \neastward over CO/KS. Once this occurs, rain is expected to \noverspread our entire region on Monday, after which time the \nassociated cold front will move through. Precipitation looks to \ngradually end from northwest to southeast on Tuesday with \nnortherly winds behind the front leading to cooler high \ntemperatures in the 60s.",
